 frame from the host view’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"frame"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" on every layout pass","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"THEOplayerRCTView.layoutSubviews","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does ","type":"text"},{"code":"player.frame = self.frame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"While the split transform is installed, the host view’s frame is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"transformed bounding box, so each pass applies the layout fraction to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"picture a SECOND time — the content renders at fraction² of its box — and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drifts the picture out of the frozen content mask, exposing black regions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside the box. react-native-video is immune: its layout stamps sublayers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"code":"bounds","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which a transform never changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The lock captures the healthy pre-transform frame at acquisition and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-asserts it (through the host’s own frame API, via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restamp"},{"type":"text","text":") whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the surface’s layer geometry deviates. Observed on the LAYER: UIView"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry setters are not KVO-compliant, CALayer’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"— the same technique as the overlay host view’s host-layer observers.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construct on the main thread (it reads and may re-stamp view geometry);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"release"},{"type":"text","text":" only invalidates the observations and is safe from any thread."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadsruntime.OptiViewAdsRuntime\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsRuntime"]]},"references":{"doc://optiviewadsruntime.OptiViewAdsRuntime/documentation/OptiViewAdsRuntime/ContentLayoutLock":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pins a host player’s internal video surface to a fixed frame while the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"split-layout reflow has a transform installed on the host view (PLAYG-513)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadsruntime.OptiViewAdsRuntime\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsRuntime\/ContentLayoutLock","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/optiviewadsruntime\/contentlayoutlock","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"ContentLayoutLock","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ContentLayoutLock"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ContentLayoutLock"}]},"doc://optiviewadsruntime.OptiViewAdsRuntime/documentation/OptiViewAdsRuntime/ContentLayoutLock/release()":{"url":"\/documentation\/optiviewadsruntime\/contentlayoutlock\/release()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadsruntime.OptiViewAdsRuntime\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsRuntime\/ContentLayoutLock\/release()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"release","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops holding the frame. The host’s next layout pass re-stamps its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry from the (by then restored) host view frame."}],"title":"release()","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://optiviewadsruntime.OptiViewAdsRuntime/documentation/OptiViewAdsRuntime/Content